    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the premier start at an elite 87.14 efficiency. Facing Paredes and his porous 4.94 xERA, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive park and platoon advantage, with his top-tier order placement cementing his status as the cornerstone of our lineup. **James Wood** (67.46) and **Brice Turang** (66.83) provide excellent supplementary value; notably, **Brice Turang** remains a primary target for stolen base accumulation due to a favorable matchup against Elder, whose slow delivery to the plate invites aggressive baserunning. While **Gabriel Moreno** and **Austin Riley** both posted strong scores exceeding 65.0, they rely heavily on exploitable SP metrics to offset middling base projections, making them essential pivots in their respective positions.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved keeping **Max Muncy** (44.18) on the bench. Despite a solid park factor against Detmers, the efficiency drop-off compared to the bottom of our active roster\u2014specifically **Henry Bolte** and **Zach McKinstry**\u2014was driven by **Max Muncy**\u2019s unfavorable slotting in the nine-hole. We are exercising caution with the **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Henry Bolte** stack against Detmers; while the park factor provides a +10% boost, Detmers\u2019 profile limits their ceiling, rendering them marginal starts. We are monitoring the lineup for **Alex Freeland**, who holds a moderate 58.23 score boosted by wind conditions, though his bottom-order placement remains a drag on his overall efficiency. Ensure game caps are managed closely, as our depth players like **Jose Caballero** and **Cole Young** are relegated to the bench to preserve limited roster space for higher-upside opportunities.",
